03:18.640 --> 03:20.280
But generally speaking,

03:20.280 --> 03:22.480
what I'm saying here is that this is great for

03:22.480 --> 03:27.080
code bases in the sense that if one person wants to use types on one file,

03:27.080 --> 03:29.960
they can, you don't have to enforce it across the entire code base,

03:29.960 --> 03:32.840
and that's the benefit of having that configured.

